### C Program: Nested Short-Circuit Condition for Voting Eligibility

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int age;
    char citizen;

    printf("Enter your age: ");
    scanf("%d", &age);

    printf("Are you an Indian citizen? (Y/N): ");
    scanf(" %c", &citizen);

    if (age >= 18 && (citizen == 'Y' || citizen == 'y'))
    {
        printf("You are eligible to vote in India.\n");
    }
    else
    {
        printf("You are not eligible to vote in India.\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

### Sample Output

```text
Enter your age: 18
Are you an Indian citizen? (Y/N): Y

You are eligible to vote in India.
```

### How it works

* `age >= 18` → checks whether the person has completed 18 years.
* `citizen == 'Y' || citizen == 'y'` → checks whether the person is an Indian citizen.
* `&&` → **both conditions must be true**.
* `||` → either `Y` or `y` is accepted.

So, **18 or above + Indian citizen = eligible to vote**.
